<title>UK: Watmoughs H1 profit down after costs.</title>
<headline>Watmoughs H1 profit down after costs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.29		   vs 9.89</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.75		   up 10 percent</p>
<p> Pretax		     9.62		   vs 10.07</p>
<p> Turnover		   105.33		 vs 93.56</p>
<p>NOTE - Printing group Watmoughs (Holdings) Plc said it anticipated little change in trading conditions in the second hald but was confident it had a sound base on which to resume growth in 1997. Pretax is after UK reorganisation costs of 1.14 million stg.</p>
<p> Operating profit	 12.52		  vs 11.82</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     1.14		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest charge	  1.92		   vs 1.98</p>
<p> Tax			  2.69		   vs 2.80</p>
<p> Net taxed		  6.93		   vs 7.27</p>
<p> Attributable	     6.75		   vs 7.09</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 8</p>
<p> Div registration date  October  8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 30</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
